      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nEnrolls the AMD mirror of Batch Invariance (Distributed) in `automatic_shard`. Its base H100 step is already enrolled. The mirror was dropped from #64272 because two of its commands differ only in env vars (`VLLM_TEST_MODEL=` OLMoE vs Granite): when the plan put them on different shards, the shard plugin matched the Granite command to OLMoE's plan entry and ran none of its tests. vllm-project/ci-infra#889 (merged) fixes that, so the mirror can shard. No commands change.\n\n## Claims\n\n| Job | Plan |\n|---|---|\n| `batch-invariance-distributed-4xh100` AMD mirror | 2 shards |\n\n- Every test of every command runs in exactly one shard, including both `VLLM_TEST_MODEL` commands when they land on different shards.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Planned with ci-infra main's planner (with #889) against main's timings: 2 shards, about 3% more machine time for the second job's setup.\n- The sharding harness (real generator, mock test tree) passes in PR mode and main mode: every test runs once.\n- `split_check.py` finds no step whose jobs each run the whole suite.\n- The mirror passed every recent main run, daily and nightly.\n- A staging build with #889's generator ran this mirror in 2 shards, OLMoE on one and Granite on the other, with the same test count as main.\n- On this head, `/ci run` (#99854) passed. The mirror was left out because its base step is nightly-only, so scoped build #99860 ran it: 2 shards, both passed with no retries, every command's passed count matches the latest main nightly (11 tests, OLMoE and Granite 1 each), machine time within 5%.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Why it was held:** the plugin found its plan entry by pytest arguments alone, and env-var prefixes aren't arguments. #889 has each shard export the command's position so the plugin picks the right entry.\n- **Timeouts unchanged.** `timeout_in_minutes` stays per job. Fallback-aware timeouts belong in a central timeout setting.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\n",
